---
/**
 * VideoCardsBlock — the `video_cards` layout: the patient-story video bands
 * that ship on / and /patient-testimonials/.
 *
 * EXTRACTED, NOT DESIGNED. Four live bands, read element for element:
 *
 *   src/pages/index.astro:249-298                       `#stories`, charcoal,
 *       `.stories-grid` three across, three PORTRAIT cards (3:4 stills,
 *       `data-video-short="true"`).
 *   src/pages/patient-testimonials/index.astro:105-213  `#veneer-stories`,
 *       sage-pale, `.veneer-stories-grid` — seven PORTRAIT cards on a six-column
 *       grid, the orphan seventh centred.
 *   src/pages/patient-testimonials/index.astro:216-265  `#stories`, charcoal,
 *       `.stories-grid` three across, three LANDSCAPE cards (4:3 stills, no
 *       `data-video-short`).
 *   src/pages/patient-testimonials/index.astro:335-373  `#featured-story`,
 *       paper, `.featured-grid` — ONE 16:9 video beside the copy column.
 *
 * ── THREE SHAPES, ONE FIELD ──────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `cardShape` is the only thing that differs between the four bands beyond
 * their words: `portrait` and `landscape` are the same card in the same grid
 * family and differ in the still's aspect, the column pattern and whether the
 * card carries `data-video-short` (the modal opens a 9:16 frame for it);
 * `featured` is the split band. Every registered value has a branch, and a
 * blank or unknown value draws `portrait` — the select's default — so a row
 * saved before anyone opened the select renders the same as one saved with it.
 *
 * `title`, `body` and `label` are drawn by the two grid shapes only; `body2`,
 * `caption` and the six button fields by the featured shape only. Those are
 * recorded here rather than hidden: a field with no rendering in a shape is
 * ignored in that shape, and wp-admin says so on the field.
 *
 * ── THE MODAL IS NOT HERE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * A `.story-card` or `.featured-video` is only a `<button data-video-id>` with
 * a play glyph. The dialog element `.story-video-modal#story-video-modal` and
 * the `is:inline` player script that opens it live in
 * src/components/StoryVideoModal.astro — page chrome, rendered ONCE per page
 * by the template outside the migration switch (and by [...slug].astro when
 * any row is a video_cards row). Two rows on one page would otherwise emit two
 * elements with the same id, and nothing under src/blocks ships a script
 * element. A page that places this row without the chrome has dead play
 * buttons; that dependency is named here and in manifest.ts so nobody "fixes"
 * it by adding a script element to this file.
 *
 * ── REVEAL ATTRIBUTES: A DOCUMENTED DEPARTURE FROM THE HOUSE SHELL ──────
 * Every other block puts `data-vs-reveal-batch` on its `<section>`. This one
 * does NOT, because the four templates never do: they batch the head's three
 * children and the cards separately (index.astro:251,:257;
 * patient-testimonials/index.astro:107,:113,:218,:224), and animations.js:34
 * staggers `[data-vs-reveal-batch] > *`. On the section the stagger would apply
 * to the one `.wrap` — one fade of the whole band instead of a per-card
 * stagger — a motion change no sweep can see. The featured shape keeps the
 * template's `data-vs-reveal` on the button and `data-vs-reveal-batch` on
 * `.featured-copy` (:344, :357).
 *
 * ── WHITESPACE IS PART OF THE MARKUP ─────────────────────────────────────
 * Measured against dist/ this week: the compressor collapses static whitespace
 * between two tags to ONE space (`</div> <div class="story-body"> <h4>`), keeps
 * a newline before a text node, and emits nothing between two flush
 * expressions. A conditional on a line of its own therefore leaves a double
 * space when it is false, and a flush `}{` chain leaves no space when it is
 * true. So every conditional element below is written flush and carries its
 * own leading `{" "}` inside its Fragment — the CalloutListBlock /
 * MediaSplitBlock idiom — which yields exactly one space whether it renders or
 * not, and the templates' bytes when every field is filled.
 *
 * ── OPTIONAL EVERYTHING, EXCEPT INSIDE `.story-body` ─────────────────────
 * A row with no YouTube code is skipped — the script ignores an empty id
 * (patient-testimonials/index.astro:288) and a card that opens nothing is a
 * broken promise. A card with no usable picture keeps its play glyph on the
 * ink-deep ground: a video without a still is still playable. `.story-body`
 * is drawn when ANY of title / body / label is set and then carries all three
 * elements, a blank one empty, so a filled card's markup is the template's to
 * the byte (the videoCardsSpec rule).
 *
 * NOTHING HERE THROWS. Same rule as PageBlocks.astro and every sibling: an
 * editor triggers deploys and never sees the output.
 *
 * Styles are co-located per docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 2.5 — every rule below names
 * the sheet and line it was copied out of, rooted at least two compounds deep
 * (memory: page CSS cannot beat block CSS — a bare `.story-card` compiles to
 * (0,2,0) and TIES `.home .story-card`).
 *
 * Spec: scratchpad plan-videoCardsSpec.md; docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md, blocks wave.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import { resolveCta } from "./cta";

/** The card's image sub-field, as wpgraphql-acf returns an ACF image. Same
    shape as ServiceCardsBlock.astro:122-128: the manifest selects
    `image { node { sourceUrl altText mediaDetails { width height } } }`. */
export interface VideoCardsImage {
  node?: {
    sourceUrl?: string | null;
    altText?: string | null;
    mediaDetails?: { width?: number | null; height?: number | null } | null;
  } | null;
}

/** One row of the layout's `video_cards` repeater. Every sub-field is optional
    at the schema level — ACF returns null for anything never saved. */
export interface VideoCard {
  /** `<h4>` on the card. Grid shapes only. */
  title?: string | null;
  /** `<p>` under the title. Grid shapes only. */
  body?: string | null;
  /** `span.label` — the hairline-prefixed capitals line. Grid shapes only. */
  label?: string | null;
  /** The YouTube id. A row without one is skipped. */
  videoId?: string | null;
  /** `data-video-title` — the iframe's accessible title in the modal. */
  videoTitle?: string | null;
  /** `aria-label` of the button. Blank derives `Play {videoTitle}`. */
  ariaLabel?: string | null;
  /** `span.featured-runtime` over the big video. Featured shape only. */
  caption?: string | null;
  /** Alt override. Falls back to the alt stored on the file in WordPress. */
  imageAlt?: string | null;
  image?: VideoCardsImage | null;
}

interface Props {
  /** DOM id, already deduplicated by PageBlocks.astro. */
  id?: string;
  /** The same value as `id`. Accepted so the spread in PageBlocks is lossless. */
  anchor?: string | null;
  /** Rail label. Read by the page that builds the rail, not by this band. */
  navLabel?: string | null;
  /** "paper" | "cream" | "sage-pale" | "sage" | "charcoal". Blank = paper. */
  band?: string | null;
  eyebrow?: string | null;
  /** May contain `<em>`, and nothing else (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md, Fact 3). */
  heading?: string | null;
  /**
   * The head paragraph on the grid shapes; the italic `p.featured-quote` on
   * the featured shape. The stored quote carries its own quotation marks —
   * this block adds none.
   */
  body?: string | null;
  /**
   * "portrait" | "landscape" | "featured". NULL, blank and anything else draw
   * `portrait` — the select's default and the shape three of the four live
   * bands ship.
   */
  cardShape?: string | null;
  /** The plain paragraph under the quote. Featured shape only. */
  body2?: string | null;
  videoCards?: (VideoCard | null)[] | null;
  /** block_cta_fields('video') minus `cta_note`. Featured shape only. */
  ctaLabel?: string | null;
  ctaHref?: string | null;
  /** Hover override. Blank falls back to ./cta.ts's destination table. */
  ctaHover?: string | null;
  ctaLabel2?: string | null;
  ctaHref2?: string | null;
  ctaHover2?: string | null;
}

/**
 * band value -> the modifier class the pages' markup already uses. The same
 * table as ServiceCardsBlock.astro:246-252, for the same reason: `alt` and
 * `dark` are inherited names, so every colour in <style> is written against
 * the band VALUE and the class is only the hook.
 *
 * The eyebrow is ALWAYS bare `.eyebrow` here, never `light`: the sage-pale
 * consumer (#veneer-stories) spells `class="eyebrow"` and paints it sage with
 * sage hairlines (patient-testimonials.css:267-274), and the charcoal consumers
 * paint --vs-eyebrow-on-sage with white hairlines (:114-121; home.css:914-916).
 * Both are stated in <style> per band; a `light` token would be a class-level
 * diff on a live band.
 */
const BAND_CLASS: Record<string, string | undefined> = {
  paper: undefined,
  cream: "cream",
  "sage-pale": "dark",
  sage: "sage",
  charcoal: "alt",
};

/**
 * `<Image>` inputs by shape — the templates' own values: index.astro:260 and
 * patient-testimonials/index.astro:116/:227 for the cards, :349-350 for the
 * featured still. Both grid shapes share one spec because both templates do.
 */
const IMAGE_SPEC = {
  card: { widths: [400, 800], sizes: "(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 33vw" },
  featured: { widths: [600, 900, 1300], sizes: "(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw" },
};

const {
  id,
  band = "paper",
  eyebrow,
  heading,
  body,
  cardShape,
  body2,
  videoCards,
  ctaLabel,
  ctaHref,
  ctaHover,
  ctaLabel2,
  ctaHref2,
  ctaHover2,
} = Astro.props;

/** Trim once, here, so every guard below tests for real content rather than for
 *  a field an editor left as a single space. */
const text = (input: unknown): string => (typeof input === "string" ? input.trim() : "");

const bandKey = typeof band === "string" && band !== "" ? band : "paper";
const bandClass = BAND_CLASS[bandKey];

/* See `cardShape` in Props: two registered values branch, everything else is
   the default. */
const shapeKey = text(cardShape);
const shape = shapeKey === "landscape" || shapeKey === "featured" ? shapeKey : "portrait";
const isFeatured = shape === "featured";
const isPortrait = shape === "portrait";

const where = `${Astro.url.pathname}${id ? ` at #${id}` : ""}`;

/**
 * CMS rows -> cards. `Array.isArray` first because an unqueried repeater
 * arrives `undefined` and one an editor never opened arrives `null`.
 *
 * The filter drops a row with no YouTube code — see the header. Everything else
 * is optional and degrades: no picture keeps the play glyph, a blank aria-label
 * derives from the video title.
 */
const allRows = (Array.isArray(videoCards) ? videoCards : []).map((row) => {
  const node = row?.image?.node ?? null;
  const src = typeof node?.sourceUrl === "string" ? node.sourceUrl : "";
  const width = node?.mediaDetails?.width ?? 0;
  const height = node?.mediaDetails?.height ?? 0;
  const videoTitle = text(row?.videoTitle);
  const title = text(row?.title);
  const cardBody = text(row?.body);
  const label = text(row?.label);

  return {
    videoId: text(row?.videoId),
    videoTitle,
    /* The field first; blank says "Play" followed by the video title, which is
       what the wp-admin instruction promises. */
    ariaLabel: text(row?.ariaLabel) || (videoTitle !== "" ? `Play ${videoTitle}` : "Play"),
    title,
    body: cardBody,
    label,
    hasBody: title !== "" || cardBody !== "" || label !== "",
    caption: text(row?.caption),
    /* Editor override first, then the alt text stored on the file itself. */
    alt: text(row?.imageAlt) || text(node?.altText),
    src,
    width,
    height,
    /* `<Image>` refuses a remote source without explicit intrinsic dimensions —
       the rule ServiceCardsBlock:462-467 and MediaSplitBlock run on. */
    hasImage: src !== "" && width > 0 && height > 0,
  };
});

const skipped = allRows.filter((card) => card.videoId === "").length;
if (skipped > 0) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] video_cards on ${where} has ${skipped} row(s) with no YouTube code — skipping those rows`,
  );
}

const playable = allRows.filter((card) => card.videoId !== "");

/* The featured shape draws the FIRST playable row only; the rest are reported,
   not silently dropped. */
if (isFeatured && playable.length > 1) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] video_cards featured on ${where} has ${playable.length} rows; only the first is drawn`,
  );
}

const rows = isFeatured ? playable.slice(0, 1) : playable;
const featured = isFeatured ? rows[0] : undefined;

const missingImages = rows.filter((card) => !card.hasImage).length;
if (missingImages > 0) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] video_cards on ${where} has ${missingImages} card(s) with no usable picture — drawing those without a still`,
  );
}

const eyebrowText = text(eyebrow);
const headingHtml = text(heading);
const bodyText = text(body);
const body2Text = text(body2);

const hasHead = eyebrowText !== "" || headingHtml !== "" || bodyText !== "";

/* The token map, hover table and resolvers live in ./cta.ts — ONE copy for
   every block that draws a CTA row. */
const cta1 = resolveCta(ctaHref, ctaHover);
const cta2 = resolveCta(ctaHref2, ctaHover2);
const label1 = text(ctaLabel);
const label2 = text(ctaLabel2);
const hasCta = label1 !== "";
const hasCta2 = label2 !== "";
const hasCtaRow = hasCta || hasCta2;

/* Button variants follow the band, the pairing GalleryMarqueeBlock.astro:200-202
   uses: light + ghost-light on the two dark bands, sage + ghost on the light
   ones — which on paper is the template's own `sage` + `ghost`
   (patient-testimonials/index.astro:367-368). */
const isDarkBand = bandKey === "charcoal" || bandKey === "sage";
const primaryVariant = isDarkBand ? "light" : "sage";
const secondaryVariant = isDarkBand ? "ghost-light" : "ghost";

const hasCopy = hasHead || body2Text !== "" || hasCtaRow;

/* The template's `aria-labelledby="featured-heading"` / `<h2 id="featured-heading">`
   pair (:335, :359), keyed off this band's id so two featured rows on one page
   cannot share a heading id. No heading, no pair: an aria-labelledby that
   points at nothing is worse than none. */
const headingId = id && headingHtml !== "" ? `${id}-heading` : undefined;
---

{isFeatured ? (
  /* patient-testimonials/index.astro:335-373. `section` and the band class are
     the block's shell tokens (the template's own `featured` token is kept);
     NO data-vs-reveal-batch on the section — see the header. */
  <section class:list={["section", bandClass, "featured"]} id={id} aria-labelledby={headingId}>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="featured-grid">{
        featured && (
          <Fragment>{" "}<button type="button" class="featured-video" data-video-id={featured.videoId} data-video-title={featured.videoTitle || undefined} aria-label={featured.ariaLabel} data-vs-reveal>{
            featured.hasImage && (
              <Fragment>{" "}<Image src={featured.src} width={featured.width} height={featured.height} alt={featured.alt} widths={IMAGE_SPEC.featured.widths} sizes={IMAGE_SPEC.featured.sizes} /></Fragment>
            )
          }
            <span class="featured-play" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
            </span>{
            featured.caption !== "" && (
              <Fragment>{" "}<span class="featured-runtime" aria-hidden="true">{featured.caption}</span></Fragment>
            )
          }
          </button></Fragment>
        )
      }{
        hasCopy && (
          <Fragment>{" "}<div class="featured-copy" data-vs-reveal-batch>{
            eyebrowText !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<span class="eyebrow">{eyebrowText}</span></Fragment>
          }{
            headingHtml !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<h2 id={headingId}><Fragment set:html={headingHtml} /></h2></Fragment>
          }{
            bodyText !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<p class="featured-quote">{bodyText}</p></Fragment>
          }{
            body2Text !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<p>{body2Text}</p></Fragment>
          }{
            hasCtaRow && (
              <Fragment>{" "}<div class="featured-actions">{
                hasCta && <Fragment>{" "}<Button variant={primaryVariant} href={cta1.href} hoverLabel={cta1.hover}>{label1}</Button></Fragment>
              }{
                hasCta2 && <Fragment>{" "}<Button variant={secondaryVariant} href={cta2.href} hoverLabel={cta2.hover}>{label2}</Button></Fragment>
              }
              </div></Fragment>
            )
          }
          </div></Fragment>
        )
      }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
) : (
  /* index.astro:249-298 and patient-testimonials/index.astro:105-213, :216-265.
     The head is `.section-head` where the templates spell `.stories-head` /
     `.veneer-stories-head`; the grid is `.video-grid.shape-*` where they spell
     `.stories-grid` / `.veneer-stories-grid` — the section-level class deltas
     every migrated band accepts. The card is the templates' to the byte. */
  <section class:list={["section", bandClass]} id={id}>
    <div class="wrap">{
      hasHead && (
        <Fragment>{" "}<div class="section-head" data-vs-reveal-batch>{
          eyebrowText !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<span class="eyebrow">{eyebrowText}</span></Fragment>
        }{
          headingHtml !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<h2><Fragment set:html={headingHtml} /></h2></Fragment>
        }{
          bodyText !== "" && <Fragment>{" "}<p>{bodyText}</p></Fragment>
        }
        </div></Fragment>
      )
    }{
      rows.length > 0 && (
        <Fragment>{" "}<div class:list={["video-grid", `shape-${shape}`]} data-vs-reveal-batch>{
          rows.map((card) => (
            <Fragment>{" "}<button type="button" class="story-card" data-video-id={card.videoId} data-video-short={isPortrait ? "true" : undefined} data-video-title={card.videoTitle || undefined} aria-label={card.ariaLabel}>
              <div class="story-photo">{
                card.hasImage && (
                  <Fragment>{" "}<Image src={card.src} width={card.width} height={card.height} alt={card.alt} widths={IMAGE_SPEC.card.widths} sizes={IMAGE_SPEC.card.sizes} /></Fragment>
                )
              }
                <span class="play-btn" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
                </span>
              </div>{
                card.hasBody && (
                  <Fragment>{" "}<div class="story-body">
                    <h4>{card.title}</h4>
                    <p>{card.body}</p>
                    <span class="label">{card.label}</span>
                  </div></Fragment>
                )
              }
            </button></Fragment>
          ))
        }
        </div></Fragment>
      )
    }
    </div>
  </section>
)}

<style>
  /* ══ WHERE THESE RULES COME FROM ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     Copied out of home.css and patient-testimonials.css with the page prefix
     stripped and each sheet's local aliases resolved back to the `--vs-*`
     tokens they alias one for one (home.css:14-38, patient-testimonials.css:12-31).

     `--shadow` is NOT one of those aliases. Both sheets define it locally as a
     two-layer shadow that is not `--vs-shadow` (home.css:30 ==
     patient-testimonials.css:23), so the card's hover shadow is written out
     literally — the same exception ServiceCardsBlock's <style> header records.

     SPECIFICITY. Astro compiles scoped rules to an ATTRIBUTE per compound, so
     a bare `.story-card` here is (0,2,0) and TIES `.home .story-card` /
     `.patient-testimonials .story-card`, leaving bundle order to decide a live
     page. Every rule below is therefore rooted under `.section` (two compounds
     minimum), and the shell itself is written `section.section` — type plus
     class, (0,2,1) — so it clears `.wp-blocks .section` and every
     `.<ns> .section.alt` at (0,3,0) rather than tying them. Same lift as
     ServiceCardsBlock's `p.svc-outro`.

     VALUES NOT COPIED FROM A SIBLING SHELL, because these bands differ from the
     family and the sheets are the authority: padding 130 not 110
     (home.css:556, patient-testimonials.css:112/:259/:322); head 820px /
     margin-bottom 60px not 760 / 64 (home.css:557, patient-testimonials.css:113/:265).

     THREE PLACES THE TWO SHEETS DISAGREE, and what won (all recorded in the
     writer's report; none is a word):
       1. `h2` type — patient-testimonials.css:51 clamp(32px,4.2vw,54px)
          line-height 1.1 (:47), home.css:61 clamp(34px,4.6vw,60px) line-height
          1.08 (:58). The family value wins (every sibling block states it;
          two of the three grid consumers sit on that sheet). Home's #stories
          heading re-sizes at migration; the words do not move.
       2. `h4` line-height — 1.1 (patient-testimonials.css:47) vs 1.08
          (home.css:58). 1.1, same reasoning.
       3. `.wrap` at ≤780 — 22px (patient-testimonials.css:520) vs home, which
          keeps 40px (home.css:41 has no 780 rule). 22px: the sheet plus the
          whole block family.

     ONE CASCADE RESULT REPRODUCED AS MEASURED, NOT AS INTENDED.
     `.patient-testimonials .featured-copy p` (0,2,1) outranks
     `.patient-testimonials .featured-quote` (0,2,0), so the quote's
     clamp(20px,2.2vw,26px) / 1.45 / 38ch / margin 26px (css:424-435) and its
     780px 18px (css:540) never render — the live quote is 15.5px / 1.8 / 52ch /
     margin-bottom 18px. The block states what renders and leaves the intended
     values to a later round that can measure the change. */

  /* ---------- band shell ----------
     home.css:556; patient-testimonials.css:112, :259-263, :320-325. `margin: 0`
     is FinalBand.astro's rule: the band owns its rhythm. */
  section.section {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 130px 0;
    background: var(--vs-paper);
  }
  section.section.cream {
    background: var(--vs-cream);
  }
  section.section.dark {
    background: var(--vs-sage-pale);
    color: var(--vs-ink);
  }
  section.section.sage {
    background: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  section.section.alt {
    background: var(--vs-charcoal-green);
  }

  /* ServiceCardsBlock.astro:863-865 — the anchor clears the nav and, on pages
     that declare one, the rail. */
  section.section[id] {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h, 77px) + var(--toc-h, 0px) + 12px);
  }

  /* home.css:41; patient-testimonials.css:34 */
  .section .wrap {
    max-width: 1240px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }

  /* ---------- section head (grid shapes) ----------
     home.css:557-563; patient-testimonials.css:113-124, :264-279. Eyebrow type
     from home.css:45-49 / patient-testimonials.css:36-40; h2 type from
     patient-testimonials.css:42-52 with the trailing ink override :554 (see the
     header for the home delta); `p` inherits the body line-height, 1.65
     (global.css body), stated so a client sheet cannot lift it. */
  .section .section-head {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto 60px;
  }
  .section .section-head .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--vs-sage);
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .section .section-head .eyebrow::before,
  .section .section-head .eyebrow::after {
    content: "";
    width: 28px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  .section .section-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--vs-ink);
    margin: 22px 0 22px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.2vw, 54px);
  }
  /* `:global()` because the `<em>` arrives through `set:html` and carries no
     scope attribute — ServiceCardsBlock.astro:897-905. */
  .section .section-head h2 :global(em) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--vs-sage-soft);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  .section .section-head p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--vs-ink-soft);
  }

  /* ---------- band inversions, head ----------
     sage-pale: patient-testimonials.css:267-279 — the eyebrow stays SAGE with
     sage hairlines (not the ink-soft a sibling shell would give it).
     charcoal: patient-testimonials.css:114-124; home.css:914-919. The sage band
